(PRC-71 — `Send signal <N> to process <pid>.` performs kill(2).
 Also covers: PRC-72 (`child` is an accepted alias for `process`), PRC-73
 (on success it CLEARS the error flag — the existence check after a
 deliberately failed reap does not re-trigger `On error`), PRC-74 (ESRCH,
 EINVAL and EPERM all set the flag and are catchable) and PRC-75 (signal 0
 delivers nothing and is the standard existence check).
 SAFETY: signal 9 goes only to the child this program forked. The two
 probes of the failure paths use signal 0, which the kernel never
 delivers: 999999 is an invalid pid (ESRCH), and pid 1 belongs to another
 user (EPERM) but receives nothing whatsoever. A generated program must
 not do even this much — see the ledger's leaf-safety column.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-71.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   no such process set the error flag
   the child alias was accepted
   an invalid signal number set the error flag
   signalling a process of another user set the error flag
   a failed reap set the error flag
   a successful signal cleared the flag
   the child was killed and reaped
)
Send signal 0 to process 999999.
On error print "no such process set the error flag".
a number called 'the child' is fork the process.
If 'the child' is 0 then, Wait 2 seconds, Exit 0.
Send signal 0 to child 'the child'.
On error print "the child alias set the error flag".
print "the child alias was accepted".
Send signal 999 to process 'the child'.
On error print "an invalid signal number set the error flag".
Send signal 0 to process 1.
On error print "signalling a process of another user set the error flag".
a number called 'the foreign reap' is reap process 999998.
On error print "a failed reap set the error flag".
Send signal 0 to child 'the child'.
On error print "the existence check errored while the flag was already set".
print "a successful signal cleared the flag".
Send signal 9 to child 'the child'.
a number called reaped is reap child 'the child'.
If reaped is 'the child' then, print "the child was killed and reaped".
